        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Soil forms at the interface of the lithosphere and the biosphere through the simultaneous action of weathering (breaking rock down) and pedogenesis (building soil structure up). Formation operates on timescales of 100 to >100,000 years, but the key insight is that loss rates under cultivation commonly exceed formation rates by 10–100×."
    },
